  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "What is the value of \\(\\dfrac{11!-10!}{9!}?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(99\\)",
    "B": "\\(100\\)",
    "C": "\\(110\\)",
    "D": "\\(121\\)",
    "E": "\\(132\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "For a positive integer \\(n\\), \\(n!\\) is the product \\(1\\cdot2\\cdots n\\). Since the denominator is \\(9!\\), expand only far enough to expose that common factor:\n\\[\n11!=11\\cdot10\\cdot9!,\\qquad 10!=10\\cdot9!.\n\\]\nBecause \\(9!>0\\), it can be canceled:\n\\[\n\\frac{11!-10!}{9!}\n=\\frac{(11\\cdot10-10)9!}{9!}\n=110-10=100.\n\\]\nThe value is \\(\\boxed{100}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
